[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="MarginContainer/ScrollContainer/Panel/MarginContainer"]
layout_mode = 2
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][b]HOW TO PLAY[/b][/center]
[hr]

[b]OBJECTIVE[/b]
Defeat the enemy [b]Leader[/b] by reducing their HP to 0.  
Summon units, control the 7×7 arena board, and use abilities, terrain, and smart positioning to win.

[hr]

[b]GAME FLOW[/b]

[b]1. DRAW PHASE[/b]
• Draw 1 card at the start of your turn.  
• If your hand is full, extra cards are discarded.

[b]2. SUMMON PHASE[/b]
• Select a card in your hand and place it on a valid tile.  
• Some cards must be summoned near your Leader.  
• Summon Abilities trigger immediately after placement.

[b]3. ACTION PHASE[/b]
Each unit may perform [i]one[/i] action:  
• Move  
• Attack  
• Use an Ability  
Multiple units may act each turn.

[b]4. END PHASE[/b]
• Regeneration, Poison, Terrain, and other effects trigger.  
• Turn passes to the opponent.

[hr]

[b]COMBAT RULES[/b]

[b]ATK & DEF[/b]  
• Attacking reduces the enemy’s DEF.  
• Survivors counterattack.  
• Units with 0 DEF are destroyed.

[b]Overflow Damage[/b]  
If a unit takes more damage than it can survive, the excess hits the [b]enemy Leader[/b].  
This makes high-ATK units and finishing blows extremely valuable.

[hr]

[b]MOVEMENT & POSITIONING[/b]

[b]Movement Types[/b]  
• Standard (1 tile)  
• Diagonal  
• Flying (can move over allies)  
• Unique patterns depending on the card

[b]Flying Units[/b]  
• Can pass over allies.  
• Landing on an enemy triggers combat.

[b]Terrain Tiles[/b]  
• Earth – Increased DEF  
• Wind – Increased movement  
• Shadow – Debuffs enemies  
• Void/Hole – Instantly kills non-flying units  

Terrain control often decides the match.

[hr]

[b]LEADER ABILITIES[/b]
Your Leader is a powerful unit with unique effects.  
Abilities unlock across 3 levels based on your Leader’s progression.

Examples:  
• Aura buffs  
• Movement boosts  
• Regeneration aura  
• Enemy debuff aura  

Position your Leader wisely — losing them ends the battle.

[hr]

[b]FUSION SYSTEM[/b]

Some cards combine into stronger units.

[b]How Fusion Works:[/b]  
1. Place a fusion-eligible unit on the board.  
2. Move or summon the second card onto it.  
3. The fusion triggers and the new unit appears.

Fusion types include:  
• Specific recipes  
• Element + Type combinations  
• Elemental synergies

[hr]

[b]ABILITY TYPES[/b]

Cards may trigger abilities:  
• On Summon  
• On Attack  
• On Take Damage  
• Turn Start / Turn End  
• Boardwide Passives  

Some require specific terrain or elemental synergies.

[hr]

[b]REWARDS & PROGRESSION[/b]

Winning battles earns:  
• New cards  
• Currency  
• New Map Nodes  
• Realm Boss progress  

Defeating Realm Bosses unlocks new realms and deck options.

[hr]

[b]CONTROLS[/b]

• Left Click – Select, move, attack, summon  
• Right Click / Cancel – Undo selection  
• Hover – View card details  
• UI Buttons – End Turn, Log, Settings

[hr]

[b]TIPS[/b]

• Establish board presence early.  
• Protect your Leader at all costs.  
• Use terrain advantages.  
• Overflow damage wins games — plan for it.  
• Fusion can swing battles; set it up intentionally.
"

